## Module 8 — Intercompany (AGIS)
**Oracle Equivalent:** Oracle Advanced Global Intercompany System

### NexusAI Pages Currently Existing
- ✅ [IntercompanyEliminations.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/IntercompanyEliminations.tsx) — 6.9KB
- ✅ [IntercompanyReconciliation.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/IntercompanyReconciliation.tsx) — 7.8KB
- ✅ `intercompany/` sub-directory — 7 pages
- ✅ [intercompany.ts](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/shared/schema/intercompany.ts) schema — Excellent: IC Batches, Headers, Lines, Transfer Pricing, Netting, Disputes

### Oracle Pages/Forms NexusAI is Missing or Partial
| Oracle Form | NexusAI Status | Gap Description |
|---|---|---|
| **IC Transaction Entry (Initiator side)** | ✅ Good | NexusAI schema and pages cover this well. |
| **Receiver Acknowledgement/Approval UI** | ⚠️ Partial | Oracle has a dedicated "Receiver Workbench" where the receiving entity approves or rejects the IC charge. |
| **IC Invoice Generation** | ❌ Missing | Oracle auto-generates AR invoices on the provider side and AP invoices on the receiver side from approved IC transactions. The backend bridge is missing. |
| **Elimination Rules Configurator** | ❌ Missing | Rules that define which account combinations are eliminated during consolidation (IC Payables vs. IC Receivables). |
| **IC Netting Settlement** | ⚠️ Partial | Session schema exists. Missing: The settlement payment generation (wire instructions to a bank or netting via AP/AR offset). |

